---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-clark-history/20261107-01/';
type Mode = 'Election Day' | 'Early Vote' | 'Mail';
type Observation = {
	year: number; native_contest: string; native_reporting_units: number;
	native_turnout: number; summed_native_registration_once_per_unit: number;
	native_footer: Record<Mode, { native_turnout: number }>;
	turnout_exceeds_registration_units: number;
};
const analysis: { observations: Observation[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const integer = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString('en-US');
---

<section id="participation-clark-history" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="clark-history-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Historical participation · Clark County, Nevada · 2020 / 2022 / 2024</p>
		<h2 id="clark-history-title">Historical precinct participation, with each statement kept separate</h2>
		<p>These are the native <strong>Turnout</strong> fields in four Clark County election
			statements, not candidate vote totals. The complete download contains all 3,894
			selected precinct-by-contest observations and their Election Day, early and mail counts.</p>
	</header>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Clark historical native statement participation">
		<table>
			<caption>Selected statements, not an independently established common electorate.
				Native registration is summed once per reporting unit; its timing and eligibility
				definition are not qualified turnout-rate denominators.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Year / statement</th><th scope="col">Native units</th>
				<th scope="col">Native registration</th><th scope="col">Native Turnout</th>
				<th scope="col">Election Day</th><th scope="col">Early Vote</th><th scope="col">Mail</th>
				<th scope="col">Units above registration</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{analysis.observations.map(row => <tr data-clark-observation={`${row.year}-${row.native_contest}`}>
				<th scope="row">{row.year} / {row.native_contest === 'PRESIDENT' ? 'President' : 'U.S. Senate'}</th>
				<td data-clark-count="native_reporting_units">{integer(row.native_reporting_units)}</td>
				<td data-clark-count="summed_native_registration_once_per_unit">{integer(row.summed_native_registration_once_per_unit)}</td>
				<td data-clark-count="native_turnout">{integer(row.native_turnout)}</td>
				{(['Election Day', 'Early Vote', 'Mail'] as Mode[]).map(mode =>
					<td data-clark-mode={mode}>{integer(row.native_footer[mode].native_turnout)}</td>)}
				<td data-clark-count="turnout_exceeds_registration_units">{integer(row.turnout_exceeds_registration_units)}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><strong>The two 2024 statements are not interchangeable.</strong> Their 915 shared
		unit participation vectors agree, but the presidential statement also includes unit
		<code>9996</code>: 42 native registrations and 40 mail participants, absent from the
		Senate statement. We do not infer why, allocate those participants or add the contests.</p>
	<p><strong>No turnout rates, cross-year precinct map or voter transitions.</strong>
		Units above registration are retained, not corrected or dropped. Matching precinct codes
		does not establish unchanged boundaries or the same people. These historical counts
		are not 2026 participation, demographic turnout, switching or measured staying home.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Originals, source checks and complete reproduction</summary>
		<p>The source is the Clark County Election Department. All eight selected PDF/Data originals,
			their full source receipts and original inventory, every selected count, CSV, exact code,
			tests and methods are included. Suppressed candidate fields stay unchanged in the originals;
			they are neither extracted nor reconstructed. Native footer percentages are preserved but unused.</p>
		<p>A separate offline check matched all 3,894 selected unit vectors and 11,682 mode counts
			to the PDFs and their printed grand controls. This is agreement between two representations
			of the same source, not independent outcome evidence. The included receipt records that
			check; rebuilding the package does not rerun it. Registration timing, a full-county ballot
			universe and cross-year geographic identity remain unqualified.</p>
		<p>The package reproduces the complete selected native-count extraction without network access.
			The original full historical collection remains available separately and unchanged.
			No personal voter records, demographic joint cells or individual scores are included.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete Clark selected originals + precinct counts + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}summary.json`} download>Clark historical statement summary + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Clark archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-clark-history { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
